module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.Meromorphic.RegularIdealSheaves
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Koszul.Defs
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Regular, Koszul-regular and `H₁`-regular ideal sheaves

Let `X` be a ringed space and `J ⊆ O_X` a sheaf of ideals.  Stacks tag 063D calls `J` *regular*,
*Koszul-regular*, *`H₁`-regular* or *quasi-regular* when every point of `Supp(O_X/J)` has an open
neighbourhood `U` on which `J` is generated by a sequence `f₁, …, f_r ∈ O_X(U)` of the
corresponding kind.  This file supplies the first three conditions, together with the two
sequence-level predicates they are built from; the quasi-regular condition is
`IsQuasiRegularIdealSheaf`, already in `RegularIdealSheaf.Basic`.

The two sequence conditions are the ones of Section 31.21:

* `f₁, …, f_r` is a *regular sequence* when multiplication by `f_i` on `O_U/(f₁, …, f_{i-1})` is
  injective as a map of sheaves, for every `i`.
* `f₁, …, f_r` is *Koszul-regular* when its Koszul complex `K_•(O_U, f_•)` is acyclic in degrees
  `> 0`, and *`H₁`-regular* when that complex is merely exact in degree `1`.

## Main definitions

* `IsRegularSequenceOn X U f`: the sections `f` form a regular sequence over `U`.
* `IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X U f P`: the Koszul complex of `f` over `U` is exact in every degree
  satisfying `P`.  Taking `P = (0 < ·)` gives Koszul-regularity and `P = (· = 1)` gives
  `H₁`-regularity, which is why the degree selector is a parameter rather than two definitions.
* `IsRegularIdealSheaf X J`, `IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf X J`, `IsH1RegularIdealSheaf X J`: parts
  (1), (2) and (3) of Stacks tag 063D.

## Main results

* `isKoszulSequenceExactOn_iff_forall_germ_isKoszulRegular` and
  `isKoszulSequenceExactOn_iff_forall_germ_isH1Regular`: the two instantiations of the degree
  selector are the germwise ring-level conditions `Koszul.IsKoszulRegular` and
  `Koszul.IsH1Regular`, so the sheaf predicates can be discharged by commutative algebra.
* `IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf.isH1RegularIdealSheaf`: the Koszul-regular condition implies the
  `H₁`-regular one, the part of the chain of Stacks tag 063E that is a degree comparison.

## Implementation notes

The regular condition is stated exactly as in the source, as monicity of the multiplication
endomorphism of `O_U/(f₁, …, f_{i-1})` furnished by `regularSequenceMultiplication`
(Stacks tag 0639); for presheaves of abelian groups monicity is sectionwise injectivity, which is
what "injective map of sheaves" means.

The Koszul condition is instead stated *germwise*, as vanishing of the homology of the ring-level
Koszul complex `Koszul.seqComplex` of the germs of `f` at each point of `U`.  This agrees with the
sheaf-level reading of the source: `K_•(O_U, f_•)` is a complex of finite free `O_U`-modules, so
its stalk at `y` is the ring-level Koszul complex of the germs of the `f_i`, and exactness of a
complex of sheaves is exactness of all its stalks.  It is also the form in which the source
computes — Lemma 31.21.1 proves the implications between the four sequence conditions by checking
stalks.  The germwise form is taken here because it rests only on `StacksDraft.RingTheory.Koszul`,
which is complete, rather than on a sheaf-level Koszul complex, which this development does not
yet have.

The degree selector is indexed by `ℕ`, matching `Koszul.seqComplex`; the source's complex vanishes
in negative degrees, so no condition is lost.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.21.2 (Tag 063D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Section 31.21 (Tag 067M)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/067M)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.3 (Tag 063E)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063E)
* [SGA 6, Exposé VII, Definition 1.4]
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular
open Stacks.RingedSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

section Sequences

/-- **A regular sequence of sections, Stacks tag 063D.** The sections `f₁, …, f_r` over `U` form a
regular sequence when for every `i` multiplication by `f_i` on `O_U/(f₁, …, f_{i-1})` is injective
as a map of sheaves, i.e. monic as an endomorphism of the underlying presheaf of abelian groups. -/
def IsRegularSequenceOn (X : RingedSpace.{u}) (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) : Prop :=
  ∀ i : Fin r, Mono
    (regularSequenceMultiplication (X.restrict U.isOpenEmbedding)
      (fun j => sectionOnRestriction X U (f j)) i).multiplication

/-- **Exactness of the Koszul complex of a sequence of sections, Stacks tag 063D.** The Koszul
complex of the sections `f₁, …, f_r` over `U` is exact in every degree satisfying `P`, expressed
germwise: at each point of `U` the ring-level Koszul complex of the germs of the `f_i` has
vanishing homology in those degrees.

`P = (0 < ·)` is Koszul-regularity of the sequence and `P = (· = 1)` is `H₁`-regularity. -/
@[ega "IV 19.1.8" "partial", sga "6 VII 1.4" "special case"]
def IsKoszulSequenceExactOn (X : RingedSpace.{u}) (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) (P : ℕ → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∀ (y : X) (hy : y ∈ U) (j : ℕ), P j →
    IsZero ((Koszul.seqComplex (germFamily X U f y hy)).homology j)

/-- Shrinking the set of degrees preserves Koszul exactness. -/
theorem IsKoszulSequenceExactOn.of_imp {X : RingedSpace.{u}} {U : Opens X} {r : ℕ}
    {f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)} {P Q : ℕ → Prop}
    (h : IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X U f Q) (hPQ : ∀ j, P j → Q j) :
    IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X U f P :=
  fun y hy j hj => h y hy j (hPQ j hj)

/-- Koszul exactness in all positive degrees is germwise Koszul-regularity of the sequence. -/
theorem isKoszulSequenceExactOn_iff_forall_germ_isKoszulRegular (X : RingedSpace.{u})
    (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) :
    IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X U f (fun j => 0 < j) ↔
      ∀ (y : X) (hy : y ∈ U), Koszul.IsKoszulRegular (germFamily X U f y hy) :=
  ⟨fun h y hy i hi => h y hy i (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hi),
    fun h y hy j hj => h y hy j (Nat.pos_iff_ne_zero.mp hj)⟩

/-- Koszul exactness in degree `1` is germwise `H₁`-regularity of the sequence. -/
theorem isKoszulSequenceExactOn_iff_forall_germ_isH1Regular (X : RingedSpace.{u})
    (U : Opens X) {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)) :
    IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X U f (fun j => j = 1) ↔
      ∀ (y : X) (hy : y ∈ U), Koszul.IsH1Regular (germFamily X U f y hy) :=
  ⟨fun h y hy => h y hy 1 rfl, fun h y hy _j hj => hj ▸ h y hy⟩

end Sequences

section IdealSheaves

/-- **Stacks tag 063D, part (1).** The ideal sheaf `J` is regular when, near every point of the
support of `O_X/J`, it is generated by a regular sequence of sections. -/
@[stacks 063D "part (1): regular ideal sheaf"]
def IsRegularIdealSheaf (X : RingedSpace.{u}) (J : (structureSheafModule X).Submodule) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X J →
    ∃ (U : Opens X) (_hx : x ∈ U) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)),
      IsRegularSequenceOn X U f ∧ IsGeneratedByOn X J U f

/-- **Stacks tag 063D, part (2).** The ideal sheaf `J` is Koszul-regular when, near every point of
the support of `O_X/J`, it is generated by a sequence whose Koszul complex is acyclic in positive
degrees. -/
@[stacks 063D "part (2): Koszul-regular ideal sheaf", sga "6 VII 1.4" "regular ideal J"]
def IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf (X : RingedSpace.{u})
    (J : (structureSheafModule X).Submodule) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X J →
    ∃ (U : Opens X) (_hx : x ∈ U) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)),
      IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X U f (fun j => 0 < j) ∧ IsGeneratedByOn X J U f

/-- **Stacks tag 063D, part (3).** The ideal sheaf `J` is `H₁`-regular when, near every point of
the support of `O_X/J`, it is generated by a sequence whose Koszul complex is exact in degree
`1`. -/
@[stacks 063D "part (3): H₁-regular ideal sheaf"]
def IsH1RegularIdealSheaf (X : RingedSpace.{u})
    (J : (structureSheafModule X).Submodule) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X J →
    ∃ (U : Opens X) (_hx : x ∈ U) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)),
      IsKoszulSequenceExactOn X U f (fun j => j = 1) ∧ IsGeneratedByOn X J U f

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 063E.**  A Koszul-regular ideal sheaf is `H₁`-regular: the local
witnesses are the same sequences, and degree `1` is a positive degree. -/
@[stacks 063E "Koszul-regular implies H₁-regular"]
theorem IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf.isH1RegularIdealSheaf {X : RingedSpace.{u}}
    {J : (structureSheafModule X).Submodule} (h : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf X J) :
    IsH1RegularIdealSheaf X J := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, r, f, hK, hG⟩ := h x hx
  exact ⟨U, hxU, r, f, hK.of_imp fun j hj => by omega, hG⟩

end IdealSheaves

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

end
